                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "listlessnesses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a319036-3b2c-33a3-8f27-859aa5bdbb76",
                        "entry_id": "b3fc9970-5a4d-3639-a8b7-bbd68fa7bc3f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being listless; apathetic indifference; lethargy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d53381a-59cf-4221-bd7e-b3369612ed4d",
                                "sense_id": "1a319036-3b2c-33a3-8f27-859aa5bdbb76",
                                "text": "But every thing must have an end. A motion made by this angelic youth, in the listlessness of going off sleep, replac'd his shirt and the bed-cloaths in a posture that shut up that treasure from longer view.",
                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "28fbb3e8-3c70-444f-af8a-bb9d0bf5a976",
                                "sense_id": "1a319036-3b2c-33a3-8f27-859aa5bdbb76",
                                "text": "This sensation of listlessness, weariness, stupidity, this disinclination to sit down and employ myself, this feeling of every thing’s being dull and insipid about the house!— I must be in love; I should be the oddest creature in the world if I were not—for a few weeks at least."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "534f9b55-abd5-4795-ac1c-77869a53fe8f",
                                "sense_id": "1a319036-3b2c-33a3-8f27-859aa5bdbb76",
                                "text": "[…] lulled into such an opium-like listlessness of vacant, unconscious reverie is this absent-minded youth by the blending cadence of waves with thoughts, that at last he loses his identity; takes the mystic ocean at his feet for the visible image of that deep, blue, bottomless soul, pervading mankind and nature; and every strange, half-seen, gliding, beautiful thing that eludes him; every dimly-discovered, uprising fin of some undiscernible form, seems to him the embodiment of those elusive thoughts that only people the soul by continually flitting through it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14ebb9dc-2224-4440-a05d-1ff9b5c10ef9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3fc9970-5a4d-3639-a8b7-bbd68fa7bc3f",
                        "source_sense_id": "1a319036-3b2c-33a3-8f27-859aa5bdbb76",
